  <prompt>
    Make `sprk_servicerequest` a first-class association target end-to-end. The entity already exists in Dataverse but has zero repo footprint — author its data-model doc and add it to the regarding machinery.

    Two halves:
    1. **Doc**: author `docs/data-model/sprk_servicerequest.md` documenting the entity (key columns, the `sprk_regardingservicerequest` lookup on `sprk_communication` created in task 001, its role as an association target).
    2. **Wiring** (additive only — MUST NOT add a new regarding mechanism, per §11 + spec MUST NOT): add a `sprk_servicerequest` entry to
       - `CommunicationService.RegardingLookupMap` (the outbound regarding-write map),
       - `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` (the client-side catalog), and
       - `IncomingAssociationResolver.RegardingFieldPriority` (the inbound resolution priority list),
       so `sprk_servicerequest` resolves through the existing polymorphic regarding path exactly like matter/project/invoice.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke full-stack engineer fluent in the ADR-024 regarding family: `RegardingLookupMap`, `RegardingFieldPriority`, `PopulateResolverFieldsAsync`, `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`, and the `docs/data-model/` doc conventions.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `docs/data-model/sprk_servicerequest.md` exists and documents the entity + its association-target role. `sprk_servicerequest` is resolvable end-to-end through the existing regarding machinery: `RegardingLookupMap`, `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`, and `RegardingFieldPriority` each have an additive `sprk_servicerequest` entry. Build clean; no new regarding mechanism introduced.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      R4 extends the Association Engine to eight targets (matter, project, invoice, service request, work assignment, event, contact, organization). `sprk_servicerequest` is one of two new targets (the other, `sprk_event`, is task 004). The entity is live in Dataverse but never documented or wired into Spaarke's regarding path. The `sprk_regardingservicerequest` lookup column is created by task 001; this task adds the doc + the code-side catalog/map/priority entries that make the lookup actually resolve.

      Component Justification §11 + spec MUST NOT: extend the existing `RegardingResolver`/`RegardingLookupMap`/`TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` — do NOT add a parallel mechanism.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_servicerequest.md (NEW)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-03: `sprk_servicerequest` MUST be resolvable end-to-end through the regarding machinery (map + catalog + priority all wired).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Extend the existing regarding family — additive entry in `RegardingLookupMap` + `RegardingFieldPriority` + `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`. Keep writing ADR-024 typed lookups + denormalized fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§11 Component Justification)">MUST NOT add a new regarding mechanism, service, or abstraction. The three existing structures are extended with one entry each.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The `sprk_regardingservicerequest` lookup column is created by task 001 — this task depends on it. Do NOT recreate the column.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Task 005 codifies the Association Engine target contract; keep the new target consistent with it.</constraint>
  </constraints>

