  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `CommunicationService.cs` `RegardingLookupMap` (~921-931) + `IncomingAssociationResolver.cs` `RegardingFieldPriority` + `PopulateResolverFieldsAsync` to see the exact existing entry shape for one target (e.g. matter/invoice).</step>
    <step order="2">Locate `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG` (grep confirms it lives in both server + client surfaces) and identify the client entry shape.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify `sprk_regardingservicerequest` column exists on `sprk_communication` (created by task 001) via Dataverse MCP `describe`. If absent, STOP — task 001 dependency not satisfied.</step>
    <step order="4">Query `sprk_servicerequest` entity metadata via MCP `describe` — capture primary name column, key columns, and any status column, to document accurately.</step>
    <step order="5">Author `docs/data-model/sprk_servicerequest.md`: entity overview, key columns, the `sprk_regardingservicerequest` lookup relationship from `sprk_communication`, and its role as association target #4. Cross-reference `sprk_communication.md`.</step>
    <step order="6">Add the additive `sprk_servicerequest` entry to `RegardingLookupMap` (→ `sprk_regardingservicerequest`), `RegardingFieldPriority` (at the correct priority tier — mirror an existing target), and `TODO_REGARDING_CATALOG`.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` — confirm clean.</step>
    <step order="8">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark task 003 ✅; confirm dependents 012/013 unblocked.</step>
    <step order="9">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute: status → completed; record the wiring entries in Decisions Made.</step>
  </steps>

