  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    `sprk_servicerequest` exists in Dataverse with zero repo footprint — this task gives it its first repo presence (doc + wiring). The lookup COLUMN is task 001's job; do not recreate it.

    This is intentionally NOT a FULL-rigor task: the `.cs` edits are additive dictionary/list entries mirroring existing targets, not logic. If, during execution, resolving `sprk_servicerequest` requires more than additive entries (e.g., a special-case in `PopulateResolverFieldsAsync`), STOP and escalate — that would be scope beyond "extend existing".

    Task 004 does the analogous wiring for `sprk_event` and also corrects the org target — kept separate because 004 touches BFF domain-match logic (FULL rigor) whereas this task is additive.
  </notes>

